{sov: Notes}
Soul-Blues Classic: Built around a succinct 16-bar minor blues structure
in A minor without a bass line on the original tracking session.

Rhythm Strumming: Accent the thumb-picked bass note on beat 1, followed
by tight fingerpicked or light-strummed triads on the higher strings.

The "I Know" Breakdown: The repeating chorus section drops down to a
percussive, vocal-heavy vamp over a steady A minor rhythm frame.

Turnaround: The shift down through Em to Dm provides the main harmonic
tension before resolving back to the main Am - Em - G - Am loop.
{eov}